  <running_head>PRO VETERI MEDICINA.</running_head>
  <bottom_margin>
    <catchword>Quam-</catchword>
  </bottom_margin>
  <main_text>
    <l n="1">lem, per unum orificium suos humo-</l>
    <l n="2">res exonerare, ex Anatomia manife-</l>
    <l n="3">stum est, adeò ut humores illi in hu-</l>
    <l n="4">mano corpore, in humano inquam</l>
    <l n="5">corpore, eo non profluant, quin sibi</l>
    <l n="6">permisceantur (in canibus enim pau-</l>
    <l n="7">lò inferior est exitus duētus pancrea-</l>
    <l n="8">tici quàm bilarii) omninò sequitur</l>
    <l n="9">succum pancreaticum &amp; bilem in in-</l>
    <l n="10">testino duodeno sibi permixta effer-</l>
    <l n="11">vescere. Unde certè elucescit adoran-</l>
    <l n="12">da Dei providentia, qui, ut utriusque</l>
    <l n="13">humoris acidi &amp; amari acredo tem-</l>
    <l n="14">peraretur, lege sancivit, ut in ipso af-</l>
    <l n="15">fluxu ad intestina sibi mutuò permi-</l>
    <l n="16">scerentur, atque, præmissa effervescen-</l>
    <l n="17">tiâ, velut prælio, alter alterius acrimo-</l>
    <l n="18">niâ frangeretur &amp; temperaretur: hinc</l>
    <l n="19">ab humano stercore non abhorrent</l>
    <l n="20">canes, quamvis aliàs fastidiant amara</l>
    <l n="21">bile infecta. Manifesto experimento</l>
    <l n="22">amaritudinem bilis quo tinctæ sunt</l>
    <l n="23">fæces humanæ à pituita &amp; succo pan-</l>
    <l n="24">creatico fractam esse.</l>
    <l n="25" para="true">Quam-</l>
  </main_text>
